{"evt":"snapshot_stored","id":"3d162358-6b12-4ef0-a3aa-d25387103e92/1","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","subject":"Build cost-flow attribution (autonomy score) into orchestrator daemon","description":"Implement token cost-flow attribution as a first-class daemon feature. Spec lives in graph notes note-mq875f7iit6 (autonomy score definition) and note-mq87hnkfo3w (cost-flow formula + moat rationale); validated prototype script at /tmp/landed_tokens.py and the cost-flow runner used on 2026-06-10 (conservation verified: prod+waste == total to the token).\n\nCore algorithm: T(n) = own_tokens(n) + inherited; distribute T(n)·w/W(n) along outgoing edges in topo order; merged nodes are sinks (claim T, pass 0); terminal non-merged nodes trap their T as named waste. Weights: blocking=1.0, context=stored context_weights (default 0.5).\n\nFour data-quality fixes the prototype exposed, all required for correct numbers:\n1. Persist merge outcomes onto graph nodes (merged flag + commit sha from merge_attempt) — today only 1/343 nodes had git info, 0 had merged status; prototype had to keyword-match commit subjects (matched 20 tasks for 3 commits — over-broad).\n2. Per-task token splits: multiple tasks sharing a session currently show identical duplicated token counts (e.g. five tasks each claiming 971,527) — split session tokens across its tasks by time windows or turn attribution.\n3. Cycle handling: 20 nodes sit in context-edge cycles — collapse strongly connected components before topo sort.\n4. Human-input denominator: count only genuinely human-typed tokens from main-session transcripts (exclude tool_results, <system-reminder>/<command-*> blocks, <task-notification>, <scheduled-task>, judge/onboarding automation prompts); estimate chars/3.8.\n\nSurface: autonomy score (Σ merged-result T ÷ human tokens), true cost per merged result (own + inherited), and top dead-end branches, via daemon endpoint + dashboard. First measured baselines for sanity: ~220× autonomy score (session-level method), 12.3% of all-time graph tokens reached merged results under the over-broad prototype sink set.","status":"completed","blockedBy":[],"owner":null,"metadata":null,"snapshotted_at":"2026-06-10T15:41:54.670Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:08:57.822Z"}
